# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# Two reasons this matters here:
#   * the official H3 skill files are verified against sha256 hashes in
#     skills/h3-prompt-writing/MANIFEST.json, so a CRLF rewrite would fail those checks;
#   * the service is deployed to Linux containers, where stray CRLF can break
#     shell scripts and the start of every file.
#
# `.ps1` stays CRLF because Windows PowerShell is the primary consumer.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be text-normalised.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
